    "question": "<p>d).</p><pre class=\"sheet\">for(k=1; k&lt;20; k+=4){\n    if(k%4==0){\n        continue;\n    }\n    if(k==17){\n        break;\n    }\n    println(k);\n    k++;\n}\nprintln(k);</pre><p><b>(2 * 4 = 8 marks)</b></p>",
    "solution": "<p>Careful: <code>k</code> goes up by 1 inside the loop (<code>k++</code>) and then by 4 in the <code>for</code>.</p><table class=\"trace\"><tr><th>k at the test</th><th>k%4 == 0?</th><th>k == 17?</th><th>Prints</th><th>Next k</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>no</td><td>no</td><td>1</td><td>1 + 1 + 4 = 6</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>no</td><td>no</td><td>6</td><td>6 + 1 + 4 = 11</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>no</td><td>no</td><td>11</td><td>11 + 1 + 4 = 16</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>yes: <code>continue</code></td><td>skipped</td><td>nothing</td><td>16 + 4 = 20</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td colspan=\"4\">20 &lt; 20 is false: the loop ends</td></tr></table><p><code>k</code> never equals 17, so <code>break</code> never runs. After the loop, <code>println(k)</code> prints 20.</p><div class=\"outbox\"><div class=\"outlab\">Exact output</div><pre>1\n6\n11\n20</pre></div>"
